{{!
    @template paygw_ifthenpay/status_page

    Outcome card shown after checkout, shared by the return and cancel pages.

    The state is said once: a status icon (or the spinner, while the return page is still waiting)
    beside the heading, and a single sentence below explaining it.

    That sentence doubles as the live region — the return page rewrites it as polling progresses —
    so the card needs no second status line.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * title - Heading; the one-line statement of what happened.
    * intro - Sentence under the heading.
    * rows - List of {label, value, strong} describing the order; strong emphasises the value.
    * actions - List of {url, text, primary} links.

    Optional context variables:
    * icon - Rendered pix icon shown beside the heading.
    * spinner - Show a spinner instead of an icon (the return page polls).
    * spinnerid / statusid - Ids the AMD module uses to update the card.
    * loadinglabel - Accessible name for the spinner.
    * retry - {id, text} button whose behaviour the AMD module owns.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Payment not completed",
        "intro": "You canceled the payment before it was completed.",
        "rows": [
            {"label": "Order reference", "value": "AbCd1234"},
            {"label": "Amount", "value": "24.50 EUR", "strong": true}
        ],
        "actions": [
            {"url": "https://example.com", "text": "Try again", "primary": true}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="container my-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-md-8 col-lg-6">
            <div class="card shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center mb-2">
                        {{! me-*/mr-* and visually-hidden/sr-only are the Bootstrap 5 and 4
                            spellings of the same thing; both are emitted so the layout holds on
                            Moodle 4.3-4.5 and on 5.x, where the BS4 name is deprecated. }}
                        {{#spinner}}
                            <span id="{{spinnerid}}" class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm text-primary me-2 mr-2 flex-shrink-0"
                                  role="status">
                                <span class="visually-hidden sr-only">{{loadinglabel}}</span>
                            </span>
                        {{/spinner}}
                        {{#icon}}
                            <span class="me-2 mr-2 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">{{{.}}}</span>
                        {{/icon}}
                        <h2 class="h4 mb-0">{{title}}</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p id="{{statusid}}" class="text-muted" {{#spinner}}aria-live="polite"{{/spinner}}>{{intro}}</p>
                    <dl class="row small mb-4">
                        {{#rows}}
                            <dt class="col-sm-5 text-muted font-weight-normal fw-normal">{{label}}</dt>
                            <dd class="col-sm-7">{{#strong}}<strong>{{/strong}}{{value}}{{#strong}}</strong>{{/strong}}</dd>
                        {{/rows}}
                    </dl>
                    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center">
                        {{#retry}}
                            {{! Deliberately not the primary action: the page checks by itself, so a
                                prominent button would suggest the customer has to do something. }}
                            <button type="button" id="{{id}}" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm me-2 mr-2">{{text}}</button>
                        {{/retry}}
                        {{#actions}}
                            <a href="{{url}}" class="btn me-2 mr-2 {{#primary}}btn-primary{{/primary}}{{^primary}}btn-link{{/primary}}">{{text}}</a>
                        {{/actions}}
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
